  "note": "V2 front-running demonstration. In v1 IntentLog anyone could commit the agent's intent hash first, the slot was taken with the wrong agent and Bond.slashByProof failed 'not in log'. Here: demo 1, a stranger commits the agent's hash under the agent's job and the chain rejects it ('not the job's agent', reverted on purpose). Demo 2, another registered agent commits the same hash under its own job: it succeeds but only fills that agent's own (agent, hash) slot. Demo 3, the real agent commits into its own slot, and demo 4 the lender, a party of the job, slashes by proof: the vendor bond pays the penalty to the treasury. Demo 5 and 6 show the missing commit case: the agent starts the job and never commits a second rogue intent, and the slash still lands because BondV2 accepts the agent's signature plus the JobBoard record that this agent's job went live. The v1 contracts in fisco-bcos.json are untouched. FISCO charges no gas price; block.timestamp is in milliseconds."
